# Sprint 11 – Vulnerability Management & Security Assessment

## Completed
- Performed a structured vulnerability assessment across the enterprise lab environment.
- Created an asset inventory for all lab systems:
  - DC01
  - SIEM01
  - WIN11-01
- Audited operating system versions, build numbers, installed security software, and system roles.
- Collected and reviewed installed Windows updates and patch history.
- Verified pending reboot status across Windows systems.
- Audited installed software using registry-based inventory methods.
- Evaluated Microsoft Defender health and protection status.
- Verified Windows Defender Firewall configuration across all network profiles.
- Reviewed local Administrator group membership for unnecessary privileged accounts.
- Audited listening network ports and validated expected enterprise services.
- Verified SMBv1 status across Windows systems.
- Audited Remote Desktop configuration and Network Level Authentication (NLA).
- Reviewed PowerShell logging configuration.
- Created a formal vulnerability findings register.
- Assigned risk ratings using a standardized severity model.
- Developed a remediation plan for identified findings.
- Remediated PowerShell Script Block Logging through Group Policy.
- Validated remediation using PowerShell and Group Policy.
- Updated vulnerability status following successful validation.
- Expanded Splunk monitoring for vulnerability-related events.
- Completed executive-level assessment documentation.

